error[K0063]: @strict block inside async fn without @strict async fn
  --> tests\ui\strict_k0063_async_context.kobo:4:9
  |
1 | async fn handler() {
  | -------------------- async fn defined here
4 |         data.borrow_mut().push(4);
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ @strict block inside async fn; borrow guards cannot cross .await
  |
why: @strict blocks create boundary guards that must be dropped before any .await point; placing an @strict block directly inside an async fn makes that rule ambiguous
fix: annotate the fn as `@strict async fn` to opt in to the async-aware guard protocol, or refactor to avoid @strict inside async context
warning[K0062]: async executor dependency is missing
  --> tests\ui\strict_k0063_async_context.kobo:2:9
  |
2 |     let data = kobo::bind(vec![1, 2, 3]);
  |         ^^^^ no async executor configured
  |
why: async code was detected but no executor dependency such as tokio or async-std was found
fix: add tokio or async-std to [dependencies] in Cargo.toml
